      "source": [
        "## 2. How Gradient Boosting Works\n",
        "\n",
        "### The Sequential Process:\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 1: Initialize**\n",
        "- Start with a constant prediction (e.g., mean for regression, log-odds for classification)\n",
        "- F_0(x) = initial_prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 2: For each iteration m = 1 to M:**\n",
        "\n",
        "1. **Calculate residuals (pseudo-residuals)**\n",
        "   - For each sample: r_i = y_i - F_{m-1}(x_i)\n",
        "   - These are the \"errors\" our current model makes\n",
        "\n",
        "2. **Fit a tree to predict residuals**\n",
        "   - Train tree h_m to predict r (not original y!)\n",
        "   - Tree learns to correct previous model's mistakes\n",
        "\n",
        "3. **Find optimal step size**\n",
        "   - γ_m = how much to trust this tree\n",
        "   - Optimizes loss function\n",
        "\n",
        "4. **Update model**\n",
        "   - F_m(x) = F_{m-1}(x) + learning_rate × γ_m × h_m(x)\n",
        "   - Add the correction to previous prediction\n",
        "\n",
        "**Step 3: Final Model**\n",
        "- F(x) = F_0(x) + Σ(learning_rate × γ_m × h_m(x))\n",
        "- Sum of all corrections\n",
        "\n",
        "### Visual Intuition:\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "Initial Prediction:  ───────── (far from truth)\n",
        "                     \n",
        "After Tree 1:        ─────↗─── (corrected a bit)\n",
        "                     \n",
        "After Tree 2:        ────↗─↗── (corrected more)\n",
        "                     \n",
        "After Tree 3:        ───↗─↗─↗─ (very close)\n",
        "                     \n",
        "...after M trees:    ≈≈≈≈≈≈≈≈≈ (almost perfect)\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "Each tree doesn't learn the original target — it learns to **fix the remaining error**."
      ]
    },
    {
