        "id": "gjoSQDvqqcyY"
      },
      "source": [
        "## 3. Pseudocode\n",
        "\n",
        "```\n",
        "BEGIN GradientBoosting\n",
        "    INPUT: Training data (X, y), number of trees M, learning_rate η\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Step 1: Initialize with constant prediction\n",
        "    F_0(x) = initialize_prediction(y)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # For classification, typically log-odds:\n",
        "    # F_0(x) = log(p / (1-p)) where p = mean(y)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    FOR m = 1 to M:\n",
        "        # Step 2: Calculate residuals (negative gradient)\n",
        "        FOR i = 1 to N:\n",
        "            # These are the errors we need to fix\n",
        "            residuals[i] = y[i] - predict_proba(F_{m-1}(x[i]))\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Step 3: Fit tree to residuals\n",
        "        h_m = DecisionTree(max_depth=d)\n",
        "        h_m.fit(X, residuals)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Step 4: Calculate leaf values\n",
        "        FOR each terminal node (leaf) j in h_m:\n",
        "            # Optimize loss for this leaf\n",
        "            gamma_{m,j} = optimal_value(samples_in_leaf_j)\n",
        "        \n",
        "        # Step 5: Update model\n",
        "        F_m(x) = F_{m-1}(x) + η × h_m(x)\n",
        "    \n",
        "    # Final prediction\n",
        "    FUNCTION predict(x):\n",
        "        logit = F_M(x)\n",
        "        probability = sigmoid(logit)\n",
        "        prediction = 1 if probability > 0.5 else 0\n",
        "        RETURN prediction\n",
        "    \n",
        "    RETURN F_M\n",
        "END\n",
        "```\n",
        "\n",
        "**Key Parameters:**\n",
        "- **n_estimators (M)**: Number of trees (typically 100-1000)\n",
        "- **learning_rate (η)**: Shrinkage parameter (0.01-0.3)\n",
        "- **max_depth**: Depth of each tree (3-8 typical)\n",
        "- **min_samples_split**: Minimum samples to split node\n",
        "- **subsample**: Fraction of samples per tree (0.5-1.0)\n",
        "- **loss**: Loss function (deviance, exponential, etc.)"
      ]
    },
